      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This directly affects my avatar which I rigged to minimize the complexity of dynamic bone.\nLooking at the antenna, the bone deformation is janked up with 2 weights. \nThis is a 3 bone chain (two in the wire one in the light) to reduce the complexity of the dynamic bone calculation weighted such that with the three bones I can get a fairly smooth bend object. \nWith the two influences, this effect falls apart. To make the avatar look correct, I'd need to make the rig more complex and the impact of the additional bones to the chain would counteract any theoretical performance gains from the 2 weights (which I can't imagine are much) and perform worse at all quality levels. \nPeople are going to rig their avatars in a way to get their desired look. If people end up having to increase the complexity of their rigs to ensure their avatars don't break on this new setting, it's going to negatively impact performance as a whole, especially on the higher settings. Based on precident, people will do that.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
